                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8780a1ca-9028-3fbc-bed9-43505b9bad84",
                        "entry_id": "f4620e15-43a2-3676-8c40-995e15c01ff4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To determine the value of (a variable or expression)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae032795-1c56-481f-a517-c98dca50cac6",
                                "sense_id": "8780a1ca-9028-3fbc-bed9-43505b9bad84",
                                "text": "As in much of biology, the most satisfying truths in ecology derive from manipulative experimentation. Tinker with nature and quantify how it responds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b8b6cda-de6e-4a66-a8b1-64ccb849c89e",
                                "sense_id": "8780a1ca-9028-3fbc-bed9-43505b9bad84",
                                "text": "Once more significant differences were observed for CTR w/o LIF. (E)- Protein levels for Hexokinase I and II, GAPDH and PKM1/2 were determined by western Blot and quantified by densiometric evaluation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf60ec14-3f80-4296-9ba1-94c1370b1b47",
                                "sense_id": "8780a1ca-9028-3fbc-bed9-43505b9bad84",
                                "text": "The most common model contains two core affect dimensions: arousal, which quantifies the intensity of the response, and valence, which quantifies the aversiveness of the situation—ranging from a very positive (pleasurable) to a very negative (aversive) emotional state."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aff7502c-5012-4bb4-9e50-47dbe93f3532",
                                "sense_id": "8780a1ca-9028-3fbc-bed9-43505b9bad84",
                                "text": "Standards for methanol extracted pigments chlorophyll a, c 2 . peridinin, β carotene, diatoxanthin and diadinoxanthin were used for quantifying pigments which were normalized per cell."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f0c2a35-1962-38b7-b116-2c843646e9ed",
                        "entry_id": "f4620e15-43a2-3676-8c40-995e15c01ff4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To relate a statement (called a predicate) to a given set using a quantifier—either for all (denoted ∀) or there exists (denoted ∃)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "106f7d76-d808-41e0-b3dd-b5909f527d42",
                                "sense_id": "1f0c2a35-1962-38b7-b116-2c843646e9ed",
                                "text": "The statement (#92;forallx#92;in#92;mathbb#123;R#125;)#92;,2x#61;x#43;x quantifies over the real numbers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
